=== <span class="anchor" id="Zace"></span><span class="anchor" id="Vietnam"></span><span class="anchor" id="Taiwan"></span> Zace (Vietnam and Taiwan) ===
The Kijang was sold in Vietnam and Taiwan under the Zace name. Introduced in Taiwan in 1988<ref>{{Cite web|title=街頭尋寶---Toyota Zace 1st. 瑞獅一代 外交車牌|url=https://www.7car.tw/articles/read/21586?k=zace|access-date=2020-07-02|website=7car.tw 小七車觀點}}</ref> the station wagon model was offered in either low roof long-wheelbase wagon with regular side-opening rear door and a high roof version lift gate variant while a pickup variant was also offered with a choice of either a 1.5L (5K)<ref name=":4">{{Cite web |title=中華汽車續命大絕招，Zinger 貨車版將重返市場、e-Veryca 正式量產商業化！|url=https://tw.news.yahoo.com/%E4%B8%AD%E8%8F%AF%E6%B1%BD%E8%BB%8A%E7%BA%8C%E5%91%BD%E5%A4%A7%E7%B5%95%E6%8B%9B-zinger-%E8%B2%A8%E8%BB%8A%E7%89%88%E5%B0%87%E9%87%8D%E8%BF%94%E5%B8%82%E5%A0%B4-e-veryca-094837896.html|access-date=2020-07-02|website=tw.news.yahoo.com|date=17 April 2020 |language=zh-Hant-TW}}</ref> or 1.8 (7K) engine. The Taiwanese market Zace wagons was offered in either 5/8 seater configurations.<ref name=":4" /> The Vietnamese market Zace only had an 8-seater configuration.

