=== <span class="anchor" id="Venture"></span><span class="anchor" id="Stallion"></span><span class="anchor" id="Stallion 1"></span><span class="anchor" id="Stallion F40"></span><span class="anchor" id="South Africa"></span> Venture/Stallion (South Africa) ===
{{redirect-distinguish-text|Toyota Venture|[[Toyota Venturer]] or [[Toyota Ventury]]}}
The Kijang was built and sold in South Africa in three body styles as the High roof station wagon Venture, or as a commercial vehicle under the Stallion nameplate available either as a panel van or pickup truck. The advertising campaign for the Stallion had local Afrikaans comedian [[Tolla van der Merwe]], and because of his popularity it is commonly called the "Tolla bakkie".<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.drivenmag.co.za/on-the-horizon-jan-2024/ |title=On the horizon |author=<!--staff--> |work=Driven |location=South Africa |date=2024-01-29}}</ref>

The Venture was available with three engine choices: a 1.8 (2Y) petrol, 2.2 (4Y) petrol, and a 2.4 (2L) diesel. Standard equipment includes Gear lock, Rear wiper and Washer, Power steering (unavailable with the 1.8 petrol engine), Air conditioning (available for 2.2-engined models only), and a ten-seat configuration. 2.2 Engine models also include an immobiliser alarm as standard (optional on 1.8 and 2.4D models) while the range-topping 2.2 GLE adds a 9-seater configuration, central locking, and makes a cassette radio standard equipment (optional on other variants). A rear differential lock is an available option for 2.4D and 2.2GLE models.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Toyota Venture|url=http://www.toyota.co.za/VENTURE/INDEX.HTML|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/19990429103457/http://www.toyota.co.za:80/VENTURE/INDEX.HTML|archive-date=April 29, 1999|access-date=2020-07-01|website=Toyota South Africa}}</ref>

The Stallion was available in either Panel van or as a Single Cab Truck with a 1.8 (2Y) petrol engine mated to a 4-Speed Manual while the 2.4 (2L) diesel was available for the pickup body style with a 5-speed manual transmission as an option. The Pickup Variants van also be optioned to be delivered as a chassis cab while the 1.8 pickup is also offered with optional 14" alloy wheels.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Toyota Stallion Key Specs (Top)|url=http://www.toyota.co.za/STALLION/KEYSPECS/TOP.HTML|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/19980701231122/http://www.toyota.co.za:80/STALLION/KEYSPECS/TOP.HTML|archive-date=1998-07-01|access-date=2020-07-02|website=Toyota South Africa}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Toyota Stallion Key Specs (Bottom)|url=http://www.toyota.co.za:80/STALLION/KEYSPECS/BOTTOM.HTML|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/19980701231130/http://www.toyota.co.za:80/STALLION/KEYSPECS/BOTTOM.HTML|archive-date=1998-07-01|access-date=2020-07-02|website=Toyota South Africa}}</ref>

