=== <span class="anchor" id="Qualis"></span><span class="anchor" id="India"></span> Qualis (India) ===
{{redirect-distinguish-text|Toyota Qualis|[[Toyota Mark II Qualis]]}}
[[File:Toyota Qualis.jpg|thumb|Toyota Qualis FS (India)]]

The third-generation Kijang was launched in India in January 2000 as Toyota's first entry into India's automobile market following a [[Toyota Kirloskar Motor|joint venture]] with the [[Kirloskar Group]] in 1997.<ref>{{Cite book|title=Information India 1997-98 And 1998-99|publisher=Concept Publishing Company|year=2002|isbn=81-7022-915-4|location=INDIA|pages=243}}</ref> The Kijang was sold in India under the Qualis name.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/products/tech.asp |title=Technical Specifications |publisher=[[Toyota Kirloskar Motor]] |year=2002 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20021021114741/http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/products/tech.asp |archive-date=2002-10-21}}</ref> The Qualis was based on the third-generation global model, but updated with front and rear styling, an updated interior making use of the switch gear, instrument cluster and rear air conditioning blower unit from the fourth-generation Kijang. Critics said the vehicle was outdated that came with an outdated design and did not expect it to sell well. However, Qualis was a hit as the vehicle was welcomed by taxi companies, fleet operators and large Indian families over others like [[Tata Motors|Tata]]'s [[Tata Sumo|Sumo]] and [[Mahindra & Mahindra|Mahindra]]'s [[Mahindra Bolero|Bolero]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Kumar |first=Abhineet |date=2013-03-12 |url=http://wap.business-standard.com/article/management/fortuner-innova-save-toyota-the-blushes-113031200568_1.html |title=Fortuner, Innova save Toyota the business |work=[[Business Standard]] |access-date=2016-06-27}}</ref>

The Qualis was initially sold only with a 2.4-litre ''[[Toyota L engine#2L-II|2L-II]]'' [[SOHC]] [[Diesel engine|diesel]] upon its introduction in 2000 in FS/GS/GST trims<ref>{{Cite web|title=Specifications - GST|url=http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/specs_gst.html|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20010107115400/http://www.toyotabharat.com:80/html/specs_gst.html|archive-date=2001-01-07|access-date=2020-07-02|publisher=Toyota |location=India}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Specifications - GS|url=http://toyotabharat.com/html/specs_gs.html|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20010210201149/http://toyotabharat.com/html/specs_gs.html|archive-date=2001-02-10|access-date=2020-07-02|publisher=Toyota |location=India}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Specifications - FS|url=http://toyotabharat.com/html/specs_fs.html|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20010210195956/http://toyotabharat.com/html/specs_fs.html|archive-date=2001-02-10|access-date=2020-07-02|publisher=Toyota |location=India}}</ref> while the [[Fuel injection|fuel-injected]] 2.0-litre ''[[Toyota RZ engine#1RZ-E|1RZ-E]]'' SOHC petrol engine was later made available in the range topping GST Super. The FS model (10-seater) is the base trim with a vinyl interior, power steering and front air conditioning (later included in refreshed models as standard) as options. The middle grade GS trim (10 seater/8 seater) gets better cloth interior with better sound deadening, power steering, front air conditioning (rear AC available as an option), and body cladding as standard with power windows and central locking offered as options. The top-end 8 seater GST<ref>{{Cite web|date=2001-02-11|title=Toyota Bharath - We have 100 answers|url=http://toyotabharat.com/Html/100answers3.html|access-date=2020-07-01|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20010211125312/http://toyotabharat.com/Html/100answers3.html|archive-date=2001-02-11}}</ref> and the petrol GST Super included front fog lamps, rear wiper and washer, wood trim, rear spoiler, alloy wheels, and all GS options as standard.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Toyota Qualis Features Archives|url=https://www.autopunditz.com/tag/toyota-qualis-features/|access-date=2020-07-01|website=Auto Punditz|language=en|archive-date=2020-07-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200701212358/https://www.autopunditz.com/tag/toyota-qualis-features/|url-status=dead}}</ref> The model range would get revamped in 2002 that brought roll down windows to the second-row doors<ref>{{Cite web|date=2002-10-21|title=Toyota :: Products :: Qualis - FS Interior|url=http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/products/qualis-FS-interior.asp|access-date=2020-07-01|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20021021112927/http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/products/qualis-FS-interior.asp|archive-date=2002-10-21}}</ref> with power windows for all four doors and central locking being standard to the now 8 seater only GS variant<ref>{{Cite web|date=2002-10-21|title=Toyota :: Products :: Qualis - GS :: Interior|url=http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/products/qualis-GS-interior.asp|access-date=2020-07-01|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20021021114729/http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/products/qualis-GS-interior.asp|archive-date=2002-10-21}}</ref> with rear AC and rear wiper and washer offered as options while the range topping GST/GST Super was replaced by a new 7-seater RS variant with captain seats.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Qualis RS - interior|url=http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/products/qualis-RS-interior.asp|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20021021121229/http://www.toyotabharat.com/html/products/qualis-RS-interior.asp|archive-date=2002-10-21|access-date=2020-07-02|publisher=Toyota |location=India}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Sharma|first=Jiveshwar|title=Toyota Qualis Brochure - Walking Down The Memory Lane|url=http://www.91wheels.com/news/toyota-qualis-brochure-walking-down-the-memory-lane|access-date=2020-07-01|website=91 wheels}}</ref>

The Qualis was discontinued in January 2005.<ref>{{cite press release |url=https://www.toyotabharat.com/news/2005/toyota-withdraws-qualis-from-indian-market.html |title=Toyota withdraws Qualis from Indian market |publisher=Toyota |location=India |date=2005-02-01 |access-date=2025-09-25}}</ref>
{{clear}}

