=== <span class="anchor" id="Unser"></span><span class="anchor" id="Malaysia"></span> Unser (F80/F82 - Malaysia) ===
The fourth-generation Kijang was sold in Malaysia as the Unser between mid-1998 to May 2005.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://autoworld.com.my/news/2005/05/31/New-INNOVAtion-FromToyota/|title=New INNOVAtion FromToyota - Autoworld.com.my|last=khong|first=ys|date=2005-05-31|work=Autoworld.com.my|access-date=2018-01-11|language=en-US}}</ref> The Unser name was derived from the German word ''unser''.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2002-12-29 |title=Toyota Unser Gets Refreshed for 2003 |url=http://autoworld.com.my/news/2002/12/29/Toyota-Unser-Gets-Refreshed-for-2003/ |website=Autoworld}}</ref> It is only offered in an 8 seater configuration with seatbelts for all three rows available as standard.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Unser - Safety|url=http://www.toyota.com.my:80/unser/unser_safety.htm|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20011006032209/http://www.toyota.com.my:80/unser/unser_safety.htm|archive-date=2001-10-06|access-date=2020-07-22|website=Toyota Malaysia}}</ref> Initially offered with either a 2.4 2L diesel engine or a 1.8 7K-E petrol engine and a 5-speed manual transmission, beginning in July 2000, an automatic variant was available with the 1.8 7K-E engine.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://autoworld.com.my/news/2000/07/14/Toyota-Unser-Auto-Now-Available/|title=Toyota Unser Auto Now Available |date=2000-07-14|work=Autoworld.com.my|access-date=2018-01-11|language=en-US}}</ref> In April 2001, a facelift was introduced. Changes included new multi-reflector headlamps, integrated spotlights into the front bumper, clear lenses with coloured bulbs for the tail lights and a new steering wheel design<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://autoworld.com.my/news/2001/04/05/Facelifted-Unser-now-in-Toyota-showrooms/|title=Facelifted Unser now in Toyota showrooms |date=2001-04-05|work=Autoworld.com.my|access-date=2018-01-11|language=en-US}}</ref> available in either petrol (GLi) or diesel trims (GLD).<ref>{{Cite web|title=Toyota Unser - Specification|url=http://www.toyota.com.my:80/unser/unser_specs03.htm|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20010429010938/http://www.toyota.com.my:80/unser/unser_specs03.htm|archive-date=2001-04-29|access-date=2020-07-22|website=Toyota Malaysia}}</ref> For 2003, the Unser was updated again and now only available with the 1.8 7K-E engine in two trim levels: GLi and LGX incorporating new exterior design, suede interior trim, 50/50 front facing third row seats (instead of a removable bench in previous models) with the new LGX trim adding power mirrors, chrome trim and body cladding.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2002-12-29|title=Toyota Unser Gets Refreshed for 2003 |language=en-US|work=Autoworld.com.my|url=http://autoworld.com.my/news/2002/12/29/Toyota-Unser-Gets-Refreshed-for-2003/|access-date=2018-01-11}}</ref>

