== Replacement ==
{{main|Toyota Avanza|Toyota IMV platform}}

Due to its diversified roles in its respective markets, the Kijang was succeeded by the [[Toyota Avanza|Avanza]] and [[Toyota IMV platform|IMV platform]] vehicles.

Toyota replaced the Kijang station wagon across Southeast Asia with the smaller [[Toyota Avanza|Avanza]] in 2003, and the larger [[Toyota Innova|Innova]] in 2004.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/cars/?Model=Kijang+Innova&code=46|title=Toyota.co.id » Cars|date=2004-12-06|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20041206222400/http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/cars/?Model=Kijang+Innova&code=46|archive-date=2004-12-06}}</ref> The latter has been retailed by [[Toyota Astra Motor]] in Indonesia as the "Kijang Innova" to retain its linkage with the original model. Therefore, Toyota categorise the three generations of the Innova as the fifth, sixth and seventh-generation Kijang.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Parwata |date=2017-10-08 |title=Toyota Kijang Sudah 6 Generasi, Kamu Pernah Lihat Enggak Generasi Pertamanya? |trans-title=The Toyota Kijang had reached 6 generations, have you seen the first generation? |url=https://otomotifnet.gridoto.com/read/231148327/toyota-kijang-sudah-6-generasi-kamu-pernah-lihat-enggak-generasi-pertamanya |access-date=2022-10-05 |website=GridOto |language=id}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Kijang History |url=https://www.toyota.co.id/corporate/history/kijang-corner |access-date=2022-10-05 |website=PT. Toyota Motor Manufacturing Indonesia |language=en |archive-date=2022-10-05  |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221005155654/https://www.toyota.co.id/corporate/history/kijang-corner |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Dananjaya |first=Dio |date=2022-11-22 |title=Alasan Toyota Masih Pakai Nama Kijang pada Innova Zenix |trans-title=The reason Toyota still uses the name Kijang on the Innova Zenix |url=https://otomotif.kompas.com/read/2022/11/22/141100215/alasan-toyota-masih-pakai-nama-kijang-pada-innova-zenix |access-date=2022-11-23 |website=Kompas.com |language=id}}</ref> The Kijang pickup was sold until early 2007,<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/cars/|title=Toyota.co.id » Cars|date=2007-01-15|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070115221451/http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/cars/|archive-date=2007-01-15}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/cars/?Model=kijang+pickup&code=23|title=Toyota.co.id » Cars|date=2006-12-15|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20061215175600/http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/cars/?Model=kijang+pickup&code=23|archive-date=2006-12-15}}</ref> when it was replaced by the Hilux pickup truck to comply with the Euro 2 emission standards.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/cars/?Model=hilux&code=98|title=Toyota.co.id » Cars|date=2007-01-23|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070123042022/http://www.toyota.astra.co.id/cars/?Model=hilux&code=98|archive-date=2007-01-23}}</ref>

The Indian market Qualis was replaced by the Innova, skipping the fourth-generation model entirely.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Jose |first=Selvin |date=2015-05-23 |title=Toyota Innova - A decade of dominance |url=https://www.autocarindia.com/car-news/toyota-innova---a-decade-of-dominance-394889 |access-date=2022-10-05 |website=Autocar India}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=M |first=Surendhar |date=2020-11-29 |title=Toyota Innova Launched In India From Rs. 6.82 Lakh... |url=https://gaadiwaadi.com/here-is-how-innovas-prices-went-up-by-300-in-15-years-across-4-updates/ |access-date=2022-10-05 |website=Gaadiwaadi.com |language=en-IN}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2005-02-01|title=Toyota set to replace Qualis with Innova|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/Toyota-set-to-replace-Qualis-with-Innova/articleshow/1008050.cms|access-date=2020-07-01|website=The Times of India|language=en}}</ref>

The Malaysian market Unser was sold alongside the Avanza introduced in late 2004<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.com.my/|title=Toyota|date=2004-10-14|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20041014081218/http://www.toyota.com.my/|archive-date=2004-10-14}}</ref> until the middle of 2005,<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.com.my/|title=Toyota|date=2005-05-22|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20050522081148/http://www.toyota.com.my/|archive-date=2005-05-22}}</ref> when it was discontinued in favor of the Innova being introduced.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.com.my/|title=Toyota|date=2005-05-25|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20050525032944/http://www.toyota.com.my/|archive-date=2005-05-25}}</ref>

The Innova was marketed in 2005 as the successor to the Revo in the Philippine market<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.com.ph/showroom/Revo/index.html|title=Toyota -"The new generation car page will be ready in February 2005"|date=2005-02-11|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20050211051428/http://www.toyota.com.ph/showroom/Revo/index.html|archive-date=2005-02-11}}</ref> with marketing material referring to the Innova as "A Beautiful [R]evolution"<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.com.ph/showroom/innova/index.html|title=Toyota - Innova|date=2005-03-06|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20050306234346/http://www.toyota.com.ph/showroom/innova/index.html|archive-date=2005-03-06}}</ref> referencing the Revo nameplate. Given the family oriented nature of the Innova, taxi and commercial businesses served previously by the entry-level DLX and GL Revo trims were now served by the Avanza, while the upmarket SR and VX trims now being catered to by the [[Toyota Fortuner|Fortuner]] SUV. Commercial variants of the Tamaraw FX were succeeded by the [[Toyota Hilux|Hilux]] FX and [[Daihatsu Gran Max|LiteAce]] FX utility vans, both carrying over the "FX" nameplate, and the Hilux Cargo closed van, along with the panel van, dropside pick-up, and aluminium van variants of the LiteAce, released in 2022.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://visor.ph/cars/you-can-now-buy-the-toyota-liteace-in-fx-and-cargo-variants/ |title=You can now buy the Toyota Liteace in FX and Cargo variants |first=Sam |last=Surla |work=Visor |location=Philippines |date=2022-08-28 |access-date=2022-09-06}}</ref> In 2024, the Tamaraw nameplate was resurrected as the nameplate for the Philippine-market [[Toyota Hilux Champ | Hilux Champ]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.topgear.com.ph/news/car-news/toyota-tamaraw-revival-ph-a4354-20230213 |title=Report: Toyota is bringing back the Tamaraw in PH |author=<!--staff--> |work=Top Gear |location=Philippines |date=2023-02-13 |access-date=2024-08-21}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.topgear.com.ph/news/car-news/next-gen-toyota-tamaraw-ph-preview-a4354-20230822 |title=This is the next-gen Toyota Tamaraw that will be assembled in PH starting 2024 |first=Leandre |last=Grecia |work=Top Gear |location=Philippines |date=2023-08-22 |access-date=2024-08-21}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Atienza |first=Isaac |date=2024-06-01 |title=Tamaraw Is Back! 2025 Toyota Tamaraw Previewed Ahead Of PH Launch |url=https://goflatoutph.com/2024/06/01/tamaraw-is-back-2025-toyota-tamaraw-previewed-ahead-of-ph-launch/ |access-date=2024-06-01 |website=Goflatoutph.com |language=en-US}}</ref>

The Taiwanese Zace Surf was replaced with the Innova<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.com.tw/showroom_INNOVA/exterior.aspx|title=Toyota Innova |date=2016-06-23|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160623220833/http://www.toyota.com.tw/showroom_INNOVA/exterior.aspx|archive-date=2016-06-23}}</ref> equipped with the 2.7 L ''[[Toyota TR engine#2TR-FE|2TR-FE]]'' petrol engine with no replacement for the four-wheel-drive variant and pickup truck. The Fortuner, then codenamed IMV4, was slated to be launched by local distributor Hotai Motors as to reflect the Zace Surf's then current lineup however due to strategic consideration by Toyota, the Innova was launched in 2007 instead with the ''2TR-FE'' to meet emission regulations with the smaller ''[[Toyota TR engine#1TR-FE|1TR-FE]]'' being introduced later to replace the larger engine. In 2016, the Innova was discontinued from the Taiwanese market with the second-generation Innova not slated to be introduced.<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://tw.iscarmg.com/index.php/top-news/home-abroad/40864-toyota-innova-2016-07-08 |script-title=zh:isCar - 台灣不玩的Toyota新車，二代Innova在印度大賣，被動安全比前一代好 |last=Lin |first=David (林大維) |work=isCar |access-date=2018-05-22 |language=zh-tw |archive-date=2018-05-23  |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180523011607/http://tw.iscarmg.com/index.php/top-news/home-abroad/40864-toyota-innova-2016-07-08 |url-status=usurped }}</ref>

The Africa/Ghana market Condor was replaced by the Fortuner in 2006,<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.co.za/models/viewrange.aspx?id=fortuner|title=Toyota South Africa|date=2006-04-20|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060420173909/http://www.toyota.co.za/models/viewrange.aspx?id=fortuner|archive-date=2006-04-20}}</ref> Avanza in 2007<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.co.za/models/viewrange.aspx?id=avanza|title=Toyota South Africa|date=2007-01-06|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070106154558/http://www.toyota.co.za/models/viewrange.aspx?id=avanza|archive-date=2007-01-06}}</ref> and Innova introduced in late 2011,<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.toyota.co.za/VehicleRange.aspx?vehicleRangeId=26|title=Innova|date=2011-10-21|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111021042328/http://www.toyota.co.za/VehicleRange.aspx?vehicleRangeId=26|archive-date=2011-10-21}}</ref> while panel van duties served by the African market Stallion were passed onto a panel van version of the Avanza<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://toyota.co.za/ranges/avanza-commercial|title=Vehicles - Avanza Commercial |website=Toyota South Africa|language=en-ZA|access-date=2017-10-18}}</ref> introduced in late 2013.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://toyota.co.za/ranges/all|title=Toyota South Africa|date=2013-09-22|access-date=2017-10-18|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130922135851/http://toyota.co.za/ranges/all|archive-date=2013-09-22}}</ref> The second-generation Innova is not introduced to the South African market due to shrinking MPV market and poor sales.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.cars.co.za/motoring_news/2016-toyota-innova---not-coming-to-sa/42450/|title=2016 Toyota Innova - Not Coming to SA|date=2016-06-08|work=Cars.co.za|access-date=2018-05-22|language=en-US}}</ref>

